<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates lower to steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates lower to steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) dipped at the short end of the curve from one week to one month, while the rest were unchanged, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The decline in the short-term PHIBOR rates followed the easing of spot rates in the money market, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 NOV 21		  NOV 20</p>
<p>    1 W		11  3/4		 11 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		11 11/16		11 13/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11  7/16		11  1/2</p>
<p>    2 M		11  7/16		11  7/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  1/2		 11  1/2</p>
<p>    6 M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    12M		11 13/16		11 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		NOV 22		  NOV 21</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8109637 Fax 8176267</p>
